{"cwd": "/sandbox/runs/harbor-dispatch/runs/eval-INC-94-r1-holdout/harbor-dispatch", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"content": "commit 435018d809a7e8ebff80330e076cedd0c0a80507\nAuthor: adage-eval <adage-eval@localhost>\nDate:   Mon Sep 28 03:40:38 2026 +0000\n\n    Fix back-to-back berth bookings being incorrectly rejected\n    \n    The overlap check was using <= instead of < comparisons, causing bookings\n    that end exactly when another starts to be considered overlapping. Changed\n    to strict inequality so that touching endpoints are not treated as overlaps.\n    \n    Fixes INC-94.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\ndiff --git a/src/berths/schedule.ts b/src/berths/schedule.ts\nindex cfd1dc4..99e9b65 100644\n--- a/src/berths/schedule.ts\n+++ b/src/berths/schedule.ts\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n import type { Booking } from \"@harbor/dispatch/types\";\n \n function overlaps(a: Booking, b: Booking): boolean {\n-  return a.start.getTime() <= b.end.getTime() && b.start.getTime() <= a.end.getTime();\n+  return a.start.getTime() < b.end.getTime() && b.start.getTime() < a.end.getTime();\n }\n \n export class BerthSchedule {\ndiff --git a/test/berths.test.ts b/test/berths.test.ts\nindex 1ed42a5..347e782 100644\n--- a/test/berths.test.ts\n+++ b/test/berths.test.ts\n@@ -41,4 +41,11 @@ describe(\"berth schedule\", () => {\n     const s = new BerthSchedule();\n     assert.throws(() => s.book({ berth: \"B1\", vessel: \"MSC Ada\", start: at(\"12:00\"), end: at(\"08:00\") }), RangeError);\n   });\n+\n+  test(\"back-to-back bookings on the same berth are allowed\", () => {\n+    const s = new BerthSchedule();\n+    s.book({ berth: \"B1\", vessel: \"MSC Ada\", start: at(\"08:00\"), end: at(\"12:00\") });\n+    s.book({ berth: \"B1\", vessel: \"Maersk Iva\", start: at(\"12:00\"), end: at(\"16:00\") });\n+    assert.equal(s.bookingsFor(\"B1\").length, 2);\n+  });\n });", "is_error": false, "tool_use_id": "toolu_0122KqbNwvmobJREAbEAvBpm", "type": "tool_result"}], "role": "user"}, "sessionId": "73f21df0-09db-4833-97d5-56ff61e79516", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:40:48.503Z", "toolUseResult": {"stdout": "commit 435018d809a7e8ebff80330e076cedd0c0a80507\nAuthor: adage-eval <adage-eval@localhost>\nDate:   Mon Sep 28 03:40:38 2026 +0000\n\n    Fix back-to-back berth bookings being incorrectly rejected\n    \n    The overlap check was using <= instead of < comparisons, causing bookings\n    that end exactly when another starts to be considered overlapping. Changed\n    to strict inequality so that touching endpoints are not treated as overlaps.\n    \n    Fixes INC-94.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\ndiff --git a/src/berths/schedule.ts b/src/berths/schedule.ts\nindex cfd1dc4..99e9b65 100644\n--- a/src/berths/schedule.ts\n+++ b/src/berths/schedule.ts\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n import type { Booking } from \"@harbor/dispatch/types\";\n \n function overlaps(a: Booking, b: Booking): boolean {\n-  return a.start.getTime() <= b.end.getTime() && b.start.getTime() <= a.end.getTime();\n+  return a.start.getTime() < b.end.getTime() && b.start.getTime() < a.end.getTime();\n }\n \n export class BerthSchedule {\ndiff --git a/test/berths.test.ts b/test/berths.test.ts\nindex 1ed42a5..347e782 100644\n--- a/test/berths.test.ts\n+++ b/test/berths.test.ts\n@@ -41,4 +41,11 @@ describe(\"berth schedule\", () => {\n     const s = new BerthSchedule();\n     assert.throws(() => s.book({ berth: \"B1\", vessel: \"MSC Ada\", start: at(\"12:00\"), end: at(\"08:00\") }), RangeError);\n   });\n+\n+  test(\"back-to-back bookings on the same berth are allowed\", () => {\n+    const s = new BerthSchedule();\n+    s.book({ berth: \"B1\", vessel: \"MSC Ada\", start: at(\"08:00\"), end: at(\"12:00\") });\n+    s.book({ berth: \"B1\", vessel: \"Maersk Iva\", start: at(\"12:00\"), end: at(\"16:00\") });\n+    assert.equal(s.bookingsFor(\"B1\").length, 2);\n+  });\n });"}, "type": "user"}
{"cwd": "/sandbox/runs/harbor-dispatch/runs/eval-INC-94-r1-holdout/harbor-dispatch", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"text": "Done! I've fixed INC-94. The issue was that the `overlaps` function in `src/berths/schedule.ts` was using `<=` comparisons instead of `<`, which incorrectly treated back-to-back bookings (where one ends exactly when another starts) as overlapping.\n\n**Summary of changes:**\n- Changed the overlap check from `<=` to `<` so that touching endpoints are not considered overlaps\n- Added a test case verifying that back-to-back bookings on the same berth are allowed\n- All 27 tests pass\n\nThe commit is now on the main branch and ready.", "type": "text"}], "id": "msg_011CfV9HzrT2ZRr1NyFnpzGE", "model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "role": "assistant"}, "sessionId": "73f21df0-09db-4833-97d5-56ff61e79516", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:40:51.507Z", "type": "assistant"}
